Renoir read-only inventory: AMD register and ATOM table definitions

Pinned source: Linux v6.19.10, commit
271f8eab9590b57a2ff0c8c9eee357723c4a85cb.
https://github.com/gregkh/linux/tree/v6.19.10/drivers/gpu/drm/amd

Adapted subset: arch/x86_64/amd/renoir_registers.h uses numeric offsets/masks
from include/asic_reg/dcn/dcn_2_1_0_offset.h and dcn_2_1_0_sh_mask.h,
include/renoir_ip_offset.h, include/asic_reg/gc/gc_9_0_offset.h,
include/asic_reg/mmhub/mmhub_1_0_offset.h and NBIF direct aliases from
include/asic_reg/nbio/nbio_7_0_offset.h, nbio_7_4_offset.h and
nbio_2_3_offset.h. Firmware table layouts/units come from
include/atomfirmware.h and include/atombios.h.

Local changes: reduced named constants; segment-plus-DWORD offsets converted
to BAR-relative bytes; an original bounded numeric parser and diagnostics.
No Linux driver, allocator, ATOM command executor or register-write function
is imported. No upstream source is downloaded by the build.

Complete notices from those definition headers follow.

